course: dictionary
lesson: 8117
title: Quick clever talk
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Repartee means quick, witty conversation, where people answer each other with clever, funny replies straight back. Think of a fast game of word ping-pong: one remark goes over the net, and a sharp reply comes straight back.
explain: Look for clues in the context. In stories and comedy, repartee shows lively, clever characters, like the nonsense talk at the Mad Hatter's tea party. Writers and comedians are admired for their repartee because it takes wit and speed.
explain: The example sentence says «support this humiliating character by repartees», where repartees means quick, clever answers. Repartee is usually talked about as one thing, so say «good repartee», not «a repartee», even though this sentence uses the plural form.
fact: Repartee is a noun. It means quick, witty conversation.
fact: Repartee is about speed and wit: the clever reply comes right back.
fact: «The Mad Hatter's tea party is full of nonsense repartee.»
fact: Repartee is usually uncountable, so say «good repartee», not «a repartee».
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning: «He is glad not to go through the town and support this humiliating character by quick, clever answers.»
exercise: The comedian's «repartee» had the whole room laughing. What is repartee? | Silent acting with no words | *Quick, witty conversation with clever, funny replies | Long speeches read from a script | A kind of dance
exercise: Find and copy the word that means quick, clever answers. «He is glad not to go through the town and support this humiliating character by repartees.» | town | through | glad | *repartees
exercise: Nadia says repartee is just talking. Why is that not quite right? | Repartee is only found in books | *Repartee is talk where the replies are quick, clever and funny | Repartee means staying silent | Repartee means talking very slowly
test: In a story, two characters trade clever, funny replies so fast that everyone laughs. What is that called? | Whispering | A long lecture | A sleepy yawn | *Repartee
test: Which sentence uses repartee correctly? | The repartee was a tall green hill. | *The two friends had quick, witty repartee all afternoon. | She repartee the sandwich quickly. | The dog repartee slept under the table.
exam: Based on this lesson, why are writers and comedians admired for their repartee? | Because it is always written in long, dull sentences | *Because it shows wit and speed in clever, lively talk | Because it only happens in the dark | Because it means silence and calm
